a concrete, step-by-step plan, and then guide you through executing that plan one directive at a time. To get started, could you please describe the software or project you'd like to build? The more detail, the better, but a high-level idea is a perfect starting point.\\\": \\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-30T02:19:26.752Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Excellent. The user has provided a clear and detailed request. This is a significant project with multiple components: a public-facing frontend, a secure backend with user authentication, a database for restricted content, and a content management system (CMS) for easy updates.\\n\\nGiven the complexity and the user's explicit desire for a system that is easy to update without coding knowledge, building this from scratch is not the optimal approach. A well-established CMS like WordPress is the most logical choice. It natively handles user roles, content management, and has a vast ecosystem of plugins for contact forms and other features.\\n\\nTo effectively plan the development of such a website, I need to build a team with specialized skills. I will recruit two Directors to lead the primary development pillars.\\n\\n1.  **Director of Engineering:** To handle the technical architecture, backend setup, security, and deployment strategy.\\n2.  **Director of Product & Design:** To focus on the user experience, site structure, and ensuring the interface is simple and intuitive, as requested.\\n\\nSimultaneously, I will send a clarification to the user. This will serve two purposes: first, to confirm my understanding of their requirements, and second, to propose the high-level strategy of using a CMS and get their buy-in before we proceed with detailed planning. This ensures alignment and prevents wasted effort.\\n\\nI will now issue three system calls: two to recruit my Directors and one to clarify the proposed approach with the user.\\n\\n###recruit-eng-director-20240520T110000Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project requires significant technical oversight, including selecting a technology stack (likely a CMS), setting up a database, implementing a secure user authentication system, and planning for deployment. A Director of Engineering is essential to lead these efforts and ensure a robust and secure final product.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-eng-director-20240520T110000Z###\\n\\n###recruit-prod-director-20240520T110001Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user has explicitly requested a 'simple and user-friendly interface'. A Director of Product & Design is needed to translate this requirement into a concrete site map, navigation flow, and visual design. This role will ensure the end product is intuitive for both public visitors and non-technical resident administrators.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Product & Design\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-prod-director-20240520T110001Z###\